DECISION ASaveIsNeverDiscriminatedByItsVersionAlone
	SPEC "The code reads a save by what it carries, never by its declared version alone: the format"
		+ "of 1.618 and earlier is recognised by its twelve parts"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/parseSaveSections.js::splitPartsCount ==="
			+ "LEGACY_SPLIT_PARTS_COUNT"
	SPEC "The releases HOLDS_FOR names are the rows of one table, in release order, each with the"
		+ "number of parts the saves it writes split into"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/gameReleases.json"
	SPEC "A declared version resolves to the last release of the table not later than it, a version"
		+ "earlier than the first release to the first release, and a version not made of"
		+ "dot-separated numbers to none"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/gameReleases.spec.js::should resolve %s to the last"
			+ "release not later than it"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/gameReleases.spec.js::should resolve %s to the first"
			+ "release"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/gameReleases.spec.js::should resolve %p to no release"
	SPEC "A save whose parts contradict the release its version resolves to raises a warning naming"
		+ "the declared version, that release and the first release whose format it carries, and is"
		+ "still read by what it carries"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/parseSaveSections.spec.js::should warn that the"
			+ "release its version declares contradicts the format it carries"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/parseSaveSections.spec.js::should still read the save"
			+ "by the format it carries"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/formatSaveWarning.spec.ts::should name the"
			+ "declared version, its release and the release whose format the save carries"
	REJECTED "Reading a save by its declared version alone: a hand-edited save contradicts its"
		+ "version"
	REJECTED "Ignoring the declared version: a contradiction would pass without a word"
		REF @OPEN_QUESTION.DeprecatedGroupIdsOfTheSkeoUpdateAreHandled
	REJECTED "Refusing a save that contradicts its version: the content is the fact, and the save"
		+ "stays readable"
	REJECTED "Leaving a version earlier than the first release unresolved: the releases before"
		+ "1.618 write its format"
	REJECTED "A list of versions of its own for each later check, such as the release that removed"
		+ "a group id: the table gains a column instead"
	RATIONALE "The version is a claim of the save, the content its fact; a contradiction is"
		+ "reported"
	SOURCE "Owner ruling"
	SOURCE "The table, the resolution of a declared version and the contradiction warning, on"
		+ "delivery of the task"
		PR 124

DECISION ColorTokenPairsMeetWcagAaByCatalog
	SPEC "Every text/background token pair the stylesheets of packages/ui-save-manager/src compose"
		+ "reaches WCAG 2.1 AA, 4.5:1, in both themes"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/styles/colors.css"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/check-color-contrast.ts::MINIMUM_CONTRAST_RATIO"
	SPEC "The pairs checked are the ones the stylesheet and its components actually compose,"
		+ "curated once from the component tree, not every declared token crossed with every other"
		IMPL "scripts/check-color-contrast.ts::TOKEN_PAIRS"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/check-color-contrast.ts::findUncataloguedForegroundDeclarations"
	SPEC "A color: declaration is covered only by a pair naming its stylesheet, its rule's selector"
		+ "and its token, the pair stating the background that selector renders on"
		IMPL "scripts/check-color-contrast.ts::isCoveredByCatalog"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/check-color-contrast.spec.ts::the background of that selector being"
			+ "uncatalogued"
	SPEC "A color: declaration names a token as var(--token); a literal or a keyword is reported"
		IMPL "scripts/check-color-contrast.ts::names no color token"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/check-color-contrast.spec.ts::as naming no color token"
	SPEC "Every stylesheet of packages/ui-save-manager/src is scanned, app.css included"
		IMPL "scripts/check-color-contrast.ts::packages/ui-save-manager/src/**/*.css"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/check-color-contrast.spec.ts::app.css included"
	REJECTED "WCAG 2.1 AAA (7:1): unreachable by the neon accent palette (--neon-pink,"
		+ "--neon-purple, --neon-cyan) without abandoning the palette's own identity"
	REJECTED "The full cross-product of every declared color token, text or not: produces pairs no"
		+ "component ever renders and would force narrowing tokens nobody sees adjacent"
	REJECTED "A one-off manual verification: the task's SPEC asks for an automated check that fails"
		+ "the build"
	REJECTED "Coverage keyed on the (token, file) pair: a second declaration of a token catalogued"
		+ "for that stylesheet passes in silence over a background nobody checked"
	REJECTED "Reading the background from the declaring rule's own background property: most text"
		+ "inherits its background from an ancestor, which a stylesheet scan cannot see"
	REJECTED "Letting inherit or currentColor through: the pair they render depends on an ancestor"
		+ "the catalog does not name for that selector"
	RATIONALE "The task's SPEC left the threshold and the verification method open. WCAG 2.1 AA is"
		+ "the widely defensible floor; the catalog is CSS-only and does not verify the actually"
		+ "-rendered DOM, a gap @TASK.CHORE91 studies closing with axe-core"
		REF @TASK.CHORE91
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FIX53
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.CHORE99
	SOURCE "the launching command's defensible-option guidance, checked against the palette before"
		+ "ratifying"
		PR 121
	SOURCE "CHORE99's delivery: the catalog keyed on the selector, literals reported, every"
		+ "stylesheet of the package scanned"
		PR 150

DECISION AHypothesisedZeroEnergyMachineIsNotAnUnknownEnergyMachine
