		+ "measurement"
		PR 120

DECISION ASaveKeepsTheFormatItWasWrittenIn
	SPEC "loading a save keeps every part it carries: no section is dropped and no index is shifted"
		+ "to bring the save to a single canonical format"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/parseSaveSections.js"
	SPEC "the format a save was read in travels with it and is the format it is written back in, so"
		+ "reading a save and writing it back reproduces the part count of the file read"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/serializeSave.js"
	SPEC "the legacy-save-format warning states that the save was written by an earlier game"
		+ "release, never that the loader adapted it"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/messages/saveWarningMessages.js"
	SPEC "the save manager and the two commands read, validate and write every format the corpus"
		+ "names, and none of them assumes one"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/SaveSectionsParserService.ts"
	REJECTED "Converting a legacy save to the current format at the user-input boundary: a merge"
		+ "whose save A was legacy then wrote a file declaring 1.618 in eleven parts, a"
		+ "contradiction our own validator warns on"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.shared_save_processing
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.cli_merge
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.cli_validate
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	RATIONALE "The canonical eleven-part format was a convenience of the loader, and it made the"
		+ "tool rewrite a file the user did not ask to convert; the corpus already describes both"
		+ "formats through INDEX and LEGACY_INDEX, so it is the code that catches up"
		REF @SECTION.TerrainLayers
		REF @DECISION.ASaveIsNeverDiscriminatedByItsVersionAlone
	SOURCE "Owner ruling, 2026-09-22, opening the wave carried by integration/save-format-preserved"

DECISION AMergedSaveTakesTheMoreRecentFormatUnlessAsked
	SPEC "when the two saves are written in different formats, the merged save is written in the"
		+ "format of the more recent of the two releases"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/mergeSaveConfigurations.ts"
	SPEC "the save manager offers a checkbox and the merge command an option, both off by default"
		+ "and both asking for the legacy format, so the two surfaces carry one polarity"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/parseMergeCliArguments.js::PREFER_LEGACY_SWITCH"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/MergeSection.tsx::preferLegacyFormat"
	SPEC "a merge whose two saves differ in format reports the format it wrote and what writing it"
		+ "dropped; the report names the option that would have kept the legacy format whenever"
		+ "that option was not applied"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/renderMergeCliOutput.js::export function renderMergeReport"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/MergeResultSection.tsx::legacyFormatCouldBeKept"
	SPEC "a merge that writes the earlier of the two formats carries the content of the later save"
		+ "unchanged and reports that a game of the earlier release may not know part of it and"
		+ "drop it on load"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/MergeSaveFiles.ts::merged-save-content-newer-than-format"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/MergeSaveFiles.spec.ts::the content the earlier"
			+ "release may not know"
	SPEC "the Terrain Layers section is written whenever the format written carries one, taken from"
		+ "save A when both saves carry it and from the save that carries it otherwise; the format"
		+ "written carrying none, it is dropped and the merge reports it"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/mergeTerrainLayers.ts"
	SPEC "the version the merged save configuration declares is the one of the save whose format is"
		+ "written"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/mergeSaveSections.ts::declaredVersion:"
			+ "writtenFormatSave.saveConfigurations[0]?.version"
	REJECTED "Declaring the release of the format written in place of a version: two saves of 2.103"
		+ "merged would declare 2.004, a patch level lost on the ordinary merge"
	REJECTED "Keeping the Terrain Layers section only when both saves carry it: a legacy merge"
		+ "asked for would lose the layers of its only legacy save"
	REJECTED "Removing from a legacy merge what the earlier release does not know: no table of the"
		+ "objects each release knows exists, and the tool would drop what the game may keep"
	REJECTED "Refusing a merge of two different formats: it blocks the use the tool exists for,"
		+ "folding an old save into a current one"
	REJECTED "Writing the format of save A without asking: the output is then not readable by the"
		+ "installed game whenever save A is the older of the two"
	RESTS_ON @RULE.SaveConfigurationComesFromSaveA
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.cli_merge
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	RATIONALE "The user knows which game release they will open the result in and the tool does"
		+ "not; the default is the one that opens in the installed game, and the report is what"
		+ "tells a user who wanted the other that the option exists"
		REF @DECISION.ASaveKeepsTheFormatItWasWrittenIn
	SOURCE "Owner ruling, 2026-09-22, opening the wave carried by integration/save-format-preserved"
	SOURCE "Owner review, 2026-09-24: asked whether a legacy merge of a current save drops what the"
		+ "earlier release does not know, and whether it warns of that loss"
		PR 127
	SOURCE "Owner's manual test in game 2.103, 2026-09-24: the legacy merge of the legacy and Skeo"
		+ "fixtures loads, is written back in the current format on save, keeps logisticsPaused"
		+ "true and drops no item; the load in 1.618 is not observed yet"
		PR 127
		REF @GAME_RELEASE.2.103
		REF @HYPOTHESIS.AGameOf1618DropsTheContentItDoesNotKnow
	ASSUMES @HYPOTHESIS.AGameOf1618DropsTheContentItDoesNotKnow

DECISION ADeprecatedGroupIdIsCarriedThroughUnchanged
	SPEC "a world object or an item whose group id a release deprecated is read, validated and"
		+ "merged like any other, and is never converted, flagged nor dropped"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/worldObjectNames.ts"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/SaveValidatorService.spec.ts::should return"
			+ "a valid result with no warning for %s"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/initMergeCli.spec.js::should write those group ids unchanged"
			+ "when the other save declares release %s"
	REJECTED "Converting Phytoplankton2 and Phytoplankton3 to the remaining phytoplankton: the game"
		+ "keeps both ids itself, so the tool would write what the game never writes"
	REJECTED "Dropping a deprecated object: it destroys content a save legitimately carries"
	REJECTED "A table of deprecated group ids by release: nothing reads it once no conversion"
		+ "happens, and the release table of FEAT89 already carries what the code tells apart"
	RESTS_ON @RULE.TheGameKeepsDeprecatedPhytoplanktonGroupIds
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	RATIONALE "The same ground as the format: the tool returns the save the user gave it, and"
		+ "rewriting a value the game itself keeps would be a conversion nobody asked for"
		REF @DECISION.ASaveKeepsTheFormatItWasWrittenIn
	SOURCE "Owner ruling, 2026-09-22, on the wave carried by integration/save-format-preserved"

DECISION EachSaveFormatIsValidatedByAWholeFileSchemaOfItsOwn
	SPEC "each save format has a whole-file schema pinned to its part count, and an entry is"
		+ "validated against the section schema that whole-file schema names at the index of the"
		+ "entry"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/validateSchemas.js::findSaveFileSchema"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/schemas/legacy-save-file.schema.json"
		ENFORCED_BY "packages/core-mapping/src/infrastructure/validateSchemas.spec.js"
	SPEC "a validation issue or a parse error located in a section carries the release whose format"
		+ "the save carries, and its location is named by the section that format gives the index"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/formatErrorLocation.ts"
		ENFORCED_BY "packages/core-mapping/src/presentation/formatErrorLocation.spec.ts"
	REJECTED "One whole-file schema loosened to admit eleven or twelve parts: it validates the"
		+ "Terrain Layers entries of a legacy save against the world events schema, or catches"
		+ "nothing"
	REJECTED "Choosing the schema by the version the save declares: a save is never discriminated"
		+ "by its version alone"
		REF @DECISION.ASaveIsNeverDiscriminatedByItsVersionAlone
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.shared_save_processing
	RESTS_ON @RULE.ALegacySaveCarriesTerrainLayersInTwelveParts
	RATIONALE "The part count decides which section sits at each index, so a validator reading the"
		+ "indexes of one format misreads the other"
	SOURCE "Owner ruling, 2026-09-23, refining FEAT93: two schemas rather than one loosened schema"
		PR 146

DECISION AMergeReportsItsFormatOnlyWhenTheTwoSavesDiffer
	SPEC "a merge of two saves of the same format leaves its warning list empty, whether or not the"
		+ "legacy format was asked for"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/MergeSaveFiles.ts::function"
			+ "reportMergedSaveFormat"
	SPEC "asking for the legacy format when both saves carry the same format writes that format"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/rules/merge/selectWrittenFormatSave.ts::return"
			+ "mainSave;"
	SPEC "the format written is chosen by comparing the releases whose formats the two saves carry,"
		+ "never by which of them carries the Terrain Layers section"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/gameReleases.js::export function compareGameReleases"
	SPEC "a warning naming a dropped section names it by its section name, never by its index nor"
		+ "its label"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/application/responses/MergeWarning.ts::section:"
			+ "SaveSectionName"
	REJECTED "Writing the legacy format for two current saves when it is asked for: the Terrain"
		+ "Layers section would be invented empty, no save carrying it"
	REJECTED "Naming a dropped section by its index: the index depends on the format, and the label"
		+ "belongs to the presentation"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	RATIONALE "The report exists to tell a user what the merge changed in the format of a save; two"
		+ "saves of one format lose nothing, and a report there would be noise on every ordinary"
		+ "merge"
		REF @DECISION.AMergedSaveTakesTheMoreRecentFormatUnlessAsked
	SOURCE "Agent ruling while implementing FEAT94, 2026-09-24"
		PR 151

DECISION ATaskBranchRunsTheAcceptanceListOfTheWorktreeInstructions
	SPEC "A task branch runs bun test, bun run lint:types, bun run check:guards, bun run"
		+ "audit:quality, awawa fmt --check . and awawa lint --strict . green before its pull"
		+ "request is opened or updated"
		IMPL "agents/worktree.md::- `bun run audit:quality`"
	SPEC "A wave launch prompt quotes the acceptance list of agents/worktree.md rather than a list"
		+ "of its own"
		IMPL "agents/worktree.md::C'est cette liste que cite le prompt de lancement d'une vague"
	REJECTED "An acceptance list held by the wave launch prompt: it omitted bun run audit:quality"
		+ "and drifted unreported"
	REJECTED "bun run check:guards as the whole local gate: the fallow audit it leaves out is a CI"
		+ "job of its own"
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.CHORE60
	RATIONALE "Two of the three pull requests of the wave of 2026-09-18 arrived red on the fallow"
		+ "CI job, the acceptance list of their prompt lacking bun run audit:quality"
	SOURCE "Usage report of pull requests 101, 102 and 103, remediation 1"
		REF @USAGE_REPORT.PR101_102_103
	SOURCE "Ruled in the pull request that delivers the task"
		PR 128

DECISION ACallerReachesASaveSectionThroughASharedFunction
	REJECTED "A read-only accessor plus a caller-side split/join to write a section back: every"
		+ "existing caller replaces a section, none only reads one, so a second function only the"
		+ "read case would use is unneeded"
	SPEC "A caller needing to replace one section of a raw save string calls"
		+ "replaceSaveSection(saveString, sectionIndex, updateSection) and never calls"
		+ "saveString.split on the section separator itself"
		IMPL "packages/shared-save-processing/replaceSaveSection.js"
