	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.shared_save_processing
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.REFACTOR62
	RATIONALE "Four call sites split a save string on '@', mutated the array at a section index and"
		+ "rejoined it by hand; a fifth caller repeating that pattern with a different mutation is"
		+ "what this closes off"
	SOURCE "Review of pull request #102, 2026-09-21, on"
		+ "packages/cli-merge/testing/fakeSaveStrings.js"
		PR 123

DECISION ADraftTaskReportsNoFindingUntilRatified
	SPEC "The gate of TASK at STATUS draft is suppressed: awawa lint --strict . exits 0 on a draft"
		+ "citing a task absent from the workspace, and exits 1 once that task is todo"
		IMPL "docs/_schema.awawa::draft: not ratified by the user, no finding reported until"
			+ "ratified"
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.CHORE63
	REJECTED "GATE warning: lint --strict promotes the L004 warning back to an error"
	REJECTED "GATE error: it refuses a draft citing a draft of a sibling branch"
	REJECTED "Per-rule gating tolerating L004 alone: awawa 2.7.0 has none"
	REJECTED "A spec spawning awawa lint on a probe corpus: no CI job installs awawa"
	RATIONALE "A draft is exploration; what it lacks or cites wrongly is reported at ratification,"
		+ "whose lint runs with the task todo"
	SOURCE "Refinement of CHORE63 with the user on 2026-09-23"
		PR 129

DECISION AReleaseIsVerifiedOnATagHoldingAVersionNumber
	SPEC "the Release workflow runs release:verify on every pushed tag whose name holds v or @"
		+ "followed by a digit, and on no other tag"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/release.yml::'**v[0-9]*'"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/release.yml::'**@[0-9]*'"
	SPEC "the release job creates a local master from origin/master before release:verify, so the"
		+ "fallow scripts keep their --base master"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/release.yml::branch master origin/master"
	REJECTED "every tag: the before-awawa rollback tag would run a release check"
	REJECTED "a release copy of the fallow scripts on --base origin/master: two copies to keep in"
		+ "step"
	RATIONALE "The tag form of a version is CHORE83's to pick; both patterns cover the forms its"
		+ "candidates write, cli-merge-v1.2.0 and cli-merge@1.2.0, and a tag checkout leaves only"
		+ "tracking references, on which --base master exits 2"
	SOURCE "Delivery of CHORE100"
		PR 133

DECISION ConsumerVersionsAreComputedByARepositoryScript
	SPEC "Only the cli-* and ui-* packages carry a version a release raises"
		IMPL "scripts/release/resolveConsumerPaths.ts::CONSUMER_PREFIXES"
	SPEC "A consumer takes a new version when a first-parent commit of master since its last tag"
		+ "changes its directory or that of a workspace package it depends on transitively"
		IMPL "scripts/release/resolveConsumerPaths.ts::collectReachableDirectories"
		IMPL "scripts/release/readCommitSubjects.ts::--first-parent"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/release/readCommitSubjects.spec.ts"
	SPEC "Below 1.0.0, a ! raises the minor number and any other subject the patch number; a"
		+ "release never leaves 0"
		IMPL "scripts/release/planRelease.ts::lowerIncrementBeforeFirstMajor"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/release/planRelease.spec.ts"
	SPEC "From 1.0.0 on, a ! raises the major number, feat the minor one, any other subject the"
		+ "patch number"
		IMPL "scripts/release/planRelease.ts::determineIncrement"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/release/planRelease.spec.ts"
	SPEC "A version is a tag <consumer>-v<version> set on master after the release pull request is"
		+ "merged"
		IMPL "scripts/release/release-tag.ts::RELEASE_BRANCH"
	SPEC "The tag of a version names the first-parent commit of master that wrote that version into"
		+ "the manifest, whatever was merged after it"
		IMPL "scripts/release/findVersionCommit.ts::--first-parent"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/release/findVersionCommit.spec.ts"
	SPEC "A release refuses a consumer whose declared version, other than 0.0.0, carries no tag"
		IMPL "scripts/release/findVersionsToTag.ts::INITIAL_VERSION"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/release/findVersionsToTag.spec.ts"
	REJECTED "release-please in manifest mode: no released version counts the paths of another"
		+ "package, so core-mapping and the shared packages would carry versions too; refactor,"
		+ "test and chore commits raise nothing; bun.lock is left stale"
	REJECTED "changesets: a file written by hand in every pull request, and a dependency that"
		+ "carries no version does not propagate its release to its dependents"
	REJECTED "Nx release and lerna-lite: both version the dependencies too, and Nx means adopting a"
		+ "build system"
	REJECTED "Deciding a bump from the scope of the commit: scopes name corpus areas and guards as"
		+ "often as packages"
	REJECTED "Starting the consumers at 1.0.0: much of the product is not settled yet"
	RATIONALE "A version exists so that a bug report names what ran; what runs is a consumer and"
		+ "every workspace package it bundles, and only the paths a commit changes say which"
	SOURCE "Ruled with the user on 2026-09-23 after the comparison CHORE83 asks for"
		PR 135

DECISION ProductionIsPublishedByHandFromAReleaseTag
	SPEC "Netlify publishes no production deploy by itself; production is the deploy of the commit"
		+ "a ui-save-manager-v* tag names, published by hand"
		IMPL "README.md::Netlify publishes no production deploy by itself"
	SPEC "Deploy previews of pull requests against master stay"
		IMPL "README.md::the deploy previews stay public"
	REJECTED "Publishing every push to master: nothing chooses what reaches production"
	REJECTED "A release branch a workflow moves to each tag and Netlify builds: a second production"
		+ "branch to keep, for a publication the owner wants to make by hand"
	REJECTED "netlify deploy --prod from GitHub Actions: an access token in the repository, and the"
		+ "server function nitro builds for Netlify is not proven to deploy that way"
	RATIONALE "Netlify cannot build a git tag, and the owner wants to control what reaches"
		+ "production; the squash commit of a release pull request is both the tagged commit and a"
		+ "deploy Netlify built from master"
	SOURCE "Ruled with the user on 2026-09-23 during CHORE83"
		PR 135

DECISION BothCliEntryFilesRunThroughOneSharedFunction
	SPEC "Running the command of a CLI when its module is the entry point, and exiting with its"
		+ "unexpected error code when the command fails, is one shared-platforms function both"
		+ "entry files call, the rendering of the failure handed to it by each CLI"
