DECISION ADependencyVersionIsHeldBackForSevenDays
	SPEC "bun install and bun add resolve no npm version published less than seven days ago, with"
		+ "no package exempted"
		IMPL "bunfig.toml::minimumReleaseAge = 604800"
	SPEC "Dependabot proposes no version less than seven days old, on both ecosystems"
		IMPL ".github/dependabot.yml::default-days: 7"
	REJECTED "Dependabot's implicit three-day cooldown: shorter than the delay bun install applies"
	REJECTED "An exclusion list: an exempted package reopens the window for the one a compromise"
		+ "targets; an urgent install passes --minimum-release-age=0 once instead"
	REJECTED "Per-bump semver cooldown days: github-actions ignores them, and the risk does not"
		+ "depend on the size of the bump"
	SOURCE "Owner request, security review of 2026-09-24"
		PR 161
		PR 162

DECISION EveryActionIsPinnedOnACommitSha
	SPEC "every uses: of .github/workflows names a full 40-character commit SHA followed by a"
		+ "comment giving the release it resolves to; a local action is exempt"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/quality.yml::fallow-rs/fallow@bd8fca5af5df4ccfd94c7a835d17bd93c31a7cef"
			+ "# v3.28.0"
		IMPL "scripts/check-action-pins.ts::findUnpinnedActions"
		ENFORCED_BY "package.json::bun run check:action-pins"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/check-action-pins.spec.ts::When a uses: names something other than a"
			+ "full commit SHA"
	SPEC "Dependabot updates a pinned action by rewriting its SHA and its same-line version comment"
		+ "together, with no configuration of its own"
		IMPL ".github/dependabot.yml::Dependabot rewrites both together"
	REJECTED "Moving major tags such as @v3: whoever moves the tag runs code in the CI, secrets"
		+ "included"
	REJECTED "Exact version tags such as @v3.28.0: a tag can be moved as well, only a commit SHA"
		+ "cannot"
	REJECTED "A SHA without its version comment: the pin reads as an opaque hash, and Dependabot"
		+ "has no version to rewrite beside it"
	SOURCE "Owner request, security review of 2026-09-24; the two Claude workflows pinned on master"
		+ "first, the rest in the task pull request"
		PR 162
		PR 163
	SOURCE "Dependabot reference, read on 2026-09-24: it updates actions referenced as"
		+ "actions/checkout@<commit>, and the version comment when it sits on the same line"
		REF @URL.DependabotSupportedEcosystemsGithubActions

DECISION AWaveIsAnEntityThatOutlivesItsTasks
	SPEC "every wave of the plan is a WAVE entity on master, carrying its MILESTONE and its BRANCH,"
		+ "and stays there once its tasks are archived and purged"
		IMPL "docs/awawa-project-methodology/waves.awawa::WAVE 8"
	SPEC "AGENTS.md and the files of agents/ name no integration branch: the base of a task is read"
		+ "from its wave"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::La base d'une tâche est le `BRANCH` de sa wave"
		IMPL "agents/worktree.md::c'est le `BRANCH` de sa wave"
	REJECTED "declaring a wave on its integration branch only: once the branch merges and its tasks"
		+ "are purged, master keeps no trace of its milestone nor of its branch"
	REJECTED "naming the base in an AGENTS.md table: the prose drifted, still naming"
		+ "integration/save-format-preserved while release-and-hardening was open"
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.CHORE116
	SOURCE "Owner request and refinement of the task, session of 2026-09-24"
		PR 170

DECISION AChangelogEntryListsOnlyUserFacingCommits
	SPEC "A changelog entry lists the commits whose subject is feat or fix, scoped or not, and"
		+ "every commit whose subject carries a !, in the order the release reads them"
		IMPL "scripts/release/addChangelogEntry.ts::commitSubjects.filter(isUserFacingChange)"
		IMPL "scripts/release/conventionalCommitSubject.ts::isUserFacingChange"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/release/addChangelogEntry.spec.ts::When the release carries commits of"
			+ "other types beside features, fixes and breaking changes"
	SPEC "An entry whose version holds no such commit reads the single line - Maintenance changes"
		+ "only"
		IMPL "scripts/release/addChangelogEntry.ts::MAINTENANCE_ONLY_LINE"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/release/addChangelogEntry.spec.ts::When the release carries no"
			+ "feature, no fix and no breaking change"
	SPEC "The filter applies to the entry alone: the version is still raised from every commit the"
		+ "tool carries since its last tag"
		IMPL "scripts/release/planRelease.ts::commitSubjects: history.commitSubjects"
		ENFORCED_BY "scripts/release/planRelease.spec.ts::When a consumer carries only maintenance"
			+ "commits"
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT120
	REJECTED "Filtering the commits when they are read: planRelease would then raise no version for"
		+ "a tool whose commits are all chore or docs, and a bug report could name a build no"
		+ "version tells apart"
	REJECTED "Listing the other commits under a Maintenance heading of their own: the entry stays"
		+ "as long, and the player still wades through dependency bumps to find the features"
	REJECTED "Leaving an entry empty when its version holds no user-facing commit: a bare heading"
		+ "reads as a release that lost its notes"
	REJECTED "Rewriting the 0.1.0 entries already published: a changelog is history, only the"
		+ "entries written from now on are filtered"
	RATIONALE "The changelog is the release note of each tool, read by a player for what changed;"
		+ "chore, docs, refactor, ci, test and build subjects say nothing to that reader, while a !"
		+ "announces a change they must know of whatever its type"
		REF @LIMITATION.AVersionTagCreatesNoGitHubRelease
	SOURCE "Owner request after reading the 0.1.0 changelog entries, ruled while delivering FEAT120"
		PR 165
		PR 171

DECISION TheFuseBoostIsCountedInTheOptimizerNotInTheMachineBreakdown
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.TEST113
	SPEC "A production breakdown entry carries the base level of its machines, without the boost of"
		+ "energy fuses"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/PlanetEnergyGrid.ts::private"
			+ "productionBreakdown(production: number)"
	SPEC "The boost of energy fuses is counted once, in the contribution of the optimizers that"
		+ "hold them, shared by fuse count when several reach one producer"
		IMPL "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/PlanetEnergyGrid.ts::contribution += totalBoost"
	REJECTED "The boost in the breakdown entries so that they alone sum to production: it would be"
		+ "counted twice, or the optimizer share would go, and with it the comparison between"
		+ "adding a machine and adding an optimizer"
	RATIONALE "The shares are indicative: they tell whether adding a machine yields more than"
		+ "adding an optimizer. The production formula they divide is confirmed by in-game"
		+ "measurements and stays"
	SOURCE "Owner ruling while refining FIX113 on 2026-09-25"

DECISION UnitTestCoverageIsGatedAtTheMeasuredFloorOfEachModule
	REJECTED "coverage = true in bunfig.toml: a filtered bun test run would fail on the modules it"
		+ "leaves out"
	REJECTED "A threshold at the suite total: Bun applies coverageThreshold to each module it"
		+ "reports and offers no total, a script summing lcov would be a gate of our own"
	REJECTED "An external coverage service: nothing leaves the repository"
	REJECTED "100 % coverage as the goal: it proves the code ran under a test, not that each use"
		+ "case is asserted, and tests written to reach it satisfy the tool and cover nothing"
	SPEC "The CI test job runs bun test --coverage, which fails when a module a unit test loads"
		+ "falls under the coverageThreshold of bunfig.toml"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/quality.yml::bun test --coverage"
		IMPL "bunfig.toml::coverageThreshold"
	SPEC "The threshold is the lowest line and function coverage measured on a module, rounded down"
		+ "to the unit, and only rises"
		IMPL "bunfig.toml::coverageThreshold = { lines = 0.29, functions = 0.0 }"
	SPEC "The coverage report of the CI test job is written to the run summary"
		IMPL ".github/workflows/quality.yml::GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY"
	SPEC "A module under the threshold is brought back by a test asserting the outcome of the use"
		+ "case its unexecuted lines serve, never by a test that only executes them: the figure"
		+ "finds untested use cases, it is not the aim"
		IMPL "bunfig.toml::The figure finds use cases no test covers, it is not the aim"
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.CHORE105
	RATIONALE "Bun reports only the modules a test loads, so the per-module floor gates a drop in"
		+ "one module and never sees a module no test imports; fallow's coverage-gaps rule covers"
		+ "that one"
		REF @DECISION.ACoverageGapExemptionIsATestRootDeclaredInOneFile
	SOURCE "Delivery of CHORE105, measured with Bun 1.4.2 on 2026-09-25"
		PR 173

DECISION ACoverageGapExemptionIsATestRootDeclaredInOneFile
	REJECTED "A fallow-ignore-file coverage-gaps directive at the top of each exempt module: the"
		+ "exemptions scatter across the code, where no one reads them as a list"
	REJECTED "A coverage-gaps severity in a fallow.toml [[overrides]] entry, or the module in"
		+ "ignoreFindings: fallow 3.27 and 3.28 ignore both for this rule"
	REJECTED "health.ignore in fallow.toml: it also removes the file from the complexity analysis"
	REJECTED "Exporting the body of a release script for a spec to import: the process test reaches"
		+ "it without widening the script"
	SPEC "A source file or export outside ui-save-manager that no test reaches statically fails the"
		+ "fallow job, over the whole project"
		IMPL "fallow.toml::coverage-gaps ="
		IMPL ".github/workflows/quality.yml::args: --coverage-gaps"
		IMPL "package.json::fallow:coverage-gaps"
	SPEC "Only a module a test runs as a spawned process, or a type declaration file, is exempt"
		IMPL "fallow-coverage-gaps.toml::entryPoints ="
	SPEC "Every exemption is an entry of fallow-coverage-gaps.toml, a fallow plugin that"
		+ "fallow.toml loads and that declares its entries test roots, each with a comment stating"
		+ "its reason"
		IMPL "fallow.toml::plugins ="
		IMPL "fallow-coverage-gaps.toml::entryPointRole ="
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.CHORE105
	RATIONALE "Bun measures only the modules a test loads; the static check is what makes an"
		+ "untested module fail. A spawned module is reached by a test fallow cannot see, and the"
		+ "owner wants the list of such modules readable in one place"
		REF @DECISION.EveryPublishedCommandHasARealProcessTest
	SOURCE "Delivery of CHORE105 and its review, fallow 3.27.0 and 3.28.0 tried on 2026-09-25"
		PR 173

DECISION ADroppedSaveIsSelectedThroughItsFileInput
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT119
	RESTS_ON @RULE.TheSaveOnPrimeBecomesSaveA
	SPEC "A dropped save is written into the file input of its area, which then reports a change;"
		+ "the drop and the pick reach the page through the same handler"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/lib/selectFileInInput.ts::input.files = selection.files;"
	SPEC "Drop areas nest, the innermost that holds as many saves as were dropped taking the drop:"
		+ "a save slot inside the merge section hands two saves on to the section"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/structure/DropZone.tsx::isInsideAnotherArea(event.currentTarget)"
	SPEC "A drop area cancels dragenter as well as dragover and announces a copy; outside every"
		+ "area the page cancels them too and announces none"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/structure/DropZone.tsx::event.dataTransfer.dropEffect"
			+ "= 'copy';"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/lib/preventDropOutsideAreas.ts::event.dataTransfer.dropEffect"
			+ "= 'none';"
	SPEC "Two saves dropped on the merge section are ordered by the code units of their names, the"
		+ "order the command's sort gives a folder"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/lib/orderDroppedSaves.ts::compareByName"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/initMergeCli.js::.filter(hasJsonExtension).sort()"
	SPEC "A single save dropped on the merge section outside both slots fills save A when it is"
		+ "empty, save B otherwise"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/MergeSection.tsx::fileA() ? saveBInput :"
			+ "saveAInput"
	REJECTED "A selection signal set by the drop beside the one set by the input: the input would"
		+ "show no file, and two paths would select a save"
	REJECTED "localeCompare for the order: it differs from the command's sort on case and accents,"
		+ "so the web UI and the command would merge a pair differently"
	REJECTED "Cancelling dragover alone: the HTML drag-and-drop model makes an element the drop"
		+ "target only when its dragenter is cancelled, so the browser shows the forbidden cursor"
		+ "and refuses the drop until the pointer moves again"
	REJECTED "A save slot refusing two saves: the slots cover most of the merge section, so two"
		+ "saves dropped on the section were refused wherever they landed"
	SOURCE "Ruled while delivering the drop of save files"
		PR 172

DECISION AnIconOnlyButtonIsNamedByItsTooltip
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT119
	SPEC "A button that shows only its icon takes its accessible name from a tooltip element it"
		+ "points at with aria-labelledby; the tooltip shows on hover and on keyboard focus"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/structure/IconButton.tsx::aria-labelledby={tooltipId}"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/styles/buttons.css::.tooltip-anchor:focus-within"
			+ ".tooltip"
		ENFORCED_BY "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/drop.e2e.ts::should show its label as a tooltip"
	SPEC "An icon-only button is drawn without a fill, in the muted text color and at the size of"
		+ "its icon, so that it stays secondary to the filled buttons that run an action"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/styles/buttons.css::.icon-button button {"
	REJECTED "The title attribute: it never shows on keyboard focus nor on touch"
	REJECTED "An aria-label beside a separate tooltip text: the two copies of one label drift apart"
		REF @DECISION.ADecorativeCharacterIsRenderedByIcon
	REJECTED "The label printed next to the icon: the owner wants the swap button to show only its"
		+ "icon"
	REJECTED "The filled primary style of the other buttons: at the height of two file inputs it"
		+ "reads as the main action and breaks the harmony of the merge section, in the owner's"
		+ "words"
	SOURCE "Owner review of the swap button"
		PR 172

DECISION ALabelledControlIsDescribedByItsTooltip
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	SPEC "A control that shows its own label and needs a longer explanation points at a tooltip"
		+ "element with aria-describedby: the visible label stays its accessible name, and the"
		+ "tooltip is read as its description"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/components/structure/CheckboxField.tsx::aria-describedby={tooltipId}"
		ENFORCED_BY "packages/ui-save-manager/e2e/merge.e2e.ts::read by a screen reader as its"
			+ "description"
	SPEC "The tooltip shows while the pointer rests on the control or its label and while the"
		+ "control holds the keyboard focus, like the tooltip of an icon-only button"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/styles/buttons.css::.tooltip-anchor:focus-within"
			+ ".tooltip"
	SPEC "The prefer-legacy checkbox of the merge section reads \"Prefer legacy format\" and its"
		+ "tooltip says what ticking it does"
		IMPL "packages/ui-save-manager/src/messages/mergeSectionMessages.js::mergeSectionPreferLegacyFormatDescription"
	REJECTED "The tooltip as the accessible name, with aria-labelledby: a screen reader would read"
		+ "the long sentence in place of the short label the page shows"
	REJECTED "The title attribute: it never shows on keyboard focus nor on touch"
	REJECTED "The explanation written in the label itself, as \"Write the legacy format of 1.618\""
		+ "was: the owner wants a short label, the detail on demand"
	RATIONALE "A sighted user reads the short label and asks for the detail; a screen reader user"
		+ "hears the name then the description, the order the page shows them in. One tooltip"
		+ "element serves both, as for an icon-only button, so the two never drift apart"
		REF @DECISION.AnIconOnlyButtonIsNamedByItsTooltip
	SOURCE "Owner review of the merge section, round 4"
		PR 172

DECISION AgentInstructionsAreWrittenInFrench
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.DOCS50
	SPEC "AGENTS.md and the files of agents/ are written in French, and AGENTS.md cites this"
		+ "decision where it states the language of the repository"
		IMPL "AGENTS.md::Ce fichier et ceux d'`agents/` restent en français"
	REJECTED "Translating them into English with the rest of the committed documentation: they are"
		+ "agent instructions read by one owner who works in French"
	RATIONALE "The general rule puts committed documentation in English; these files are the one"
		+ "exception, and without a decision only their own prose held it"
	SOURCE "Owner ruling while refining DOCS50 on 2026-09-25"
		PR 179

DECISION TheRootCliScriptsRunTheirEntryPointDirectly
	SPEC "the root merge and validate scripts run the entry point of their package directly, as the"
		+ "node: scripts do, never through bun run --filter"
		IMPL "package.json::\"merge\": \"bun packages/cli-merge/cli/merge-cli.js\""
		IMPL "package.json::\"validate\": \"bun packages/cli-validate/cli/validate-cli.js\""
		ENFORCED_BY "packages/cli-merge/cli/merge-cli.version.spec.js::the root script of Bun"
		ENFORCED_BY "packages/cli-validate/cli/validate-cli.version.spec.js::the root script of Bun"
	SPEC "the merge reads the folders of the input directory in name order and reports each one, a"
		+ "skipped folder included, under a Processing line naming it"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/initMergeCli.js::(await readDirectory(inputDir)).sort()"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/initMergeCli.js::renderProcessingFolder(folder);"
	SPEC "the empty line before the path of the written save goes to stderr, and only when the"
		+ "block of the folder holds a warning"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/initMergeCli.js::function hasReport"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/renderMergeCliOutput.js::export function renderReportSeparator"
	SPEC "the block of each folder opens on an empty line, written to stderr before its Processing"
		+ "line"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/renderMergeCliOutput.js::export function"
			+ "renderProcessingFolder"
	SPEC "stdout holds one line per written save, its path behind a tick, as bun validate announces"
		+ "a valid save"
		IMPL "packages/cli-merge/cli/renderMergeCliOutput.js::console.log(`✓ ${outputPath}`);"
	REJECTED "bun run --filter cli-merge merge: it prefixes every line with the workspace and"
		+ "script names and prints its own progress and exit-code lines, stdout included, so stdout"
		+ "no longer holds the lines of the written saves alone"
	REJECTED "run.silent in the root bunfig.toml: it would hide the command echoed by every script"
		+ "of the workspace, and bun run --filter would still add its prefixes"
	REJECTED "Writing the empty line to stdout: stdout would no longer hold the lines of the"
		+ "written saves alone"
	REJECTED "An empty line before every path, warnings or not: a folder with nothing to report"
		+ "would show its path detached from its Processing line"
	REJECTED "The bare path on stdout: the owner asked for a tick before it, and bun validate"
		+ "already announces its verdict behind one on stdout"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.cli_merge
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.cli_validate
	APPLIES_TO_TASK @TASK.FEAT114
	RATIONALE "bun run echoes the command of the script it runs, as it does for the node: scripts;"
		+ "that one line is the package manager's under both runtimes, every other line is the"
		+ "command's own"
	SOURCE "Agent ruling while implementing FEAT114, 2026-09-25, amended by the owner's review of"
		+ "the pull request for the tick and the empty line opening each block"
		PR 182
